1
00:00:00,125 --> 00:00:00,965
The first thing she did

2
00:00:00,965 --> 00:00:01,949
was to call me

3
00:00:01,949 --> 00:00:04,799
and thank me for the contribution

4
00:00:04,799 --> 00:00:05,739
I had in her life.

5
00:00:05,829 --> 00:00:06,809
Hi, I'm Syaheer.

6
00:00:06,809 --> 00:00:10,169
I've been an MAP Coach since 2011,

7
00:00:10,169 --> 00:00:11,245
which is about 15 years ago.

8
00:00:11,345 --> 00:00:13,023
Hi, I'm Nur Azyyati.

9
00:00:13,023 --> 00:00:15,115
Teaching has always been my passion.

10
00:00:15,225 --> 00:00:16,445
I used to be an educator,

11
00:00:16,445 --> 00:00:19,125
so I've moved out to IT

12
00:00:19,125 --> 00:00:20,177
in corporate roles.

13
00:00:20,177 --> 00:00:22,422
And this is my way of giving back.

14
00:00:22,427 --> 00:00:24,167
I want to help those, especially students

15
00:00:24,167 --> 00:00:27,127
who need more guidance and support.

16
00:00:27,232 --> 00:00:28,492
I get to interact

17
00:00:28,492 --> 00:00:29,492
with a lot of students

18
00:00:29,492 --> 00:00:31,832
and I've touched many lives.

19
00:00:31,882 --> 00:00:33,642
It's fulfilling to see students

20
00:00:33,642 --> 00:00:35,302
who initially struggle,

21
00:00:35,302 --> 00:00:37,062
doubt themselves or lack motivation

22
00:00:37,062 --> 00:00:38,142
slowly begin to believe

23
00:00:38,142 --> 00:00:39,206
in their own abilities.

24
00:00:39,231 --> 00:00:40,711
When I meet them outside now,

25
00:00:40,711 --> 00:00:42,009
they are doing well.

26
00:00:42,009 --> 00:00:43,719
Before this, they were actually

27
00:00:43,719 --> 00:00:47,281
not very confident about themselves.

28
00:00:47,281 --> 00:00:49,316
Back in 2024, I was teaching

29
00:00:49,316 --> 00:00:50,854
a Primary 6 Foundation student.

30
00:00:50,854 --> 00:00:52,140
She has to retake her PSLE.

31
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:53,060
She told me that

32
00:00:53,060 --> 00:00:55,155
this is the last time.

33
00:00:55,155 --> 00:00:57,040
She worked really, really hard.

34
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:58,800
She actually passed

35
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:00,827
her Math Foundation

36
00:01:00,827 --> 00:01:01,863
for the first time.

37
00:01:01,863 --> 00:01:03,383
I hope my students walk away

38
00:01:03,383 --> 00:01:05,403
with greater confidence in themselves

39
00:01:05,403 --> 00:01:06,843
and believe that they are capable

40
00:01:06,843 --> 00:01:08,837
of achieving more than they think.

41
00:01:08,837 --> 00:01:10,877
You don't have to be a perfect educator

42
00:01:10,877 --> 00:01:12,713
because I think every human makes mistakes.

43
00:01:12,713 --> 00:01:14,713
As long as you are passionate,

44
00:01:14,713 --> 00:01:15,353
you have the patience

45
00:01:15,353 --> 00:01:17,373
and you are willing to have

46
00:01:17,373 --> 00:01:18,812
an impact on a child's life.

47
00:01:18,842 --> 00:01:21,142
If you are already thinking about it,

48
00:01:21,142 --> 00:01:21,832
sign up.
